Package: rk-pw-camera
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, pipewire, wireplumber, v4l-utils
Recommends: camera-engine-rkaiq-rk3576 | camera-engine-rkaiq
Description: PipeWire camera for Rockchip vendor-kernel ISPs
 The Rockchip vendor kernel's ISP (rkisp) only offers the V4L2
 multi-planar capture API, which PipeWire's V4L2 monitor cannot use, so
 desktop camera apps such as GNOME Snapshot and browsers see no camera.
 .
 rk-pw-camera publishes the ISP main path that has a sensor behind it
 as a PipeWire camera, streaming only while an application uses it, and
 hides the ~50 internal rkcif/rkisp/rkvpss nodes from WirePlumber.
 Image quality needs the Rockchip 3A server (camera-engine-rkaiq).
